"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative launched on June 15th with Sarah Tan as the lead. The initial phase one budget was $500,000, which was later adjusted to $550,000 to cover real-time analytics integration. The executive board subsequently approved a total budget of $2 million for all phases. Key milestones include the completion of the testing phase (celebrated on October 10th) and a breakthrough in predictive analytics in phase two. The team has expanded with Mike Chen and Lisa Ray, and a compliance plan budget of $55,000 has been allocated. There are also early-stage discussions regarding a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology. A detailed report on phase two progress will be presented on November 20th."
